From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Omer Dangoor <omerdn1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:58:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mcp): echo only the caller's env in the run tool's result

The run tool's result listed env_vars as the caller's env plus every
non-empty MAESTRO_* variable from the server's own environment, which
withInjectedShellEnvVars adds for the flows. Those variables belong to
whoever started the server, and the result handed all of them to the agent
that called the tool.

The flows still get the shell's MAESTRO_* variables as before. The result
now lists only the env the caller passed, and leaves env_vars out when the
caller passed none.

withInjectedShellEnvVars and RunTool.handle take the shell environment as
a parameter, defaulting to System.getenv(), so the tests can set one.
---
 .../java/maestro/cli/mcp/tools/RunTool.kt     | 15 +--
 .../maestro/cli/mcp/tools/RunToolTest.kt      | 94 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../main/java/maestro/orchestra/util/Env.kt   |  6 +-
 3 files changed, 107 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

